I will provide you with the content of a document that has been partially read by OCR (so it may contain errors).
Your task is to write a title for the document in paperless-ngx, so that it is easy to find in a list.
If the original title is already adding value and not just a technical filename you can use it as extra information to enhance your suggestion.
Respond only with the title, without any additional information. The content is likely in {{.Language}}.

Title format: <date> <issuer> - <what it is> - <person>
- <date>: the document's own date as YYYY-MM (year and month), or YYYY when only the year matters (annual statement, tax year, diploma). Leave it out for a document without a date of its own (brochure, ID card).
- <issuer>: the short name of the organisation that issued the document, without legal suffixes (Siemens Industry Software, not Siemens Industry Software Netherlands B.V.; IND, Belastingdienst, Medical Park). For a document the household wrote, the organisation it is for.
- <what it is>: a few words in Turkish (with Turkish letters) saying what the document is, with the document's own key term in parentheses when it helps searching: "Maaş bordrosu (Loonstrook)", "Kan tahlili sonucu", "Oturum izni (Verblijfsvergunning)", "Trafik cezası", "İş sözleşmesi".
- <person>: the first name of the household member it is about (Sercan, Melike, Kaan), or of the relative for a family member's document. Leave it out when it is about several people or nobody.
Examples:
2024-06 Medical Park - Kan tahlili sonucu - Kaan
2023-12 Siemens Industry Software - Maaş bordrosu (Loonstrook) - Sercan
2022 Siemens Industry Software - Yıllık gelir özeti (Jaaropgave) - Sercan
IND - Oturum kartı (Verblijfsdocument) - Melike
2024-02 CJIB - Trafik cezası

The data will be provided using an XML-like format for clarity:

<original_title>{{.Title}}</original_title>
<content>
{{.Content}}
